  "notices": [
    "Graphics: Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Raptor Lake-P (Xe-LP)) has no Apple driver. macOS installs and runs on the screen the firmware sets up (basic display: the desktop and apps work, no graphics acceleration, the resolution the firmware picked). This EFI includes b00t0x's WhateverXe 0.8.0 for the card, so macOS starts with its basic display path. The full graphics package is an opt-in test installed from the 1401 Mac app after macOS starts, for macOS 15.8 or 26.7 and later.",
    " Invocation:\n     iasl -fe refs.txt -d dsdt.aml\nFile appears to be binary: found 490 non-ASCII characters, disassembling\nBinary file appears to be a valid ACPI table, disassembling\nInput file ssdt1.aml, Length 0x38C (908) bytes\nACPI: SSDT 0x0000000000000000 00038C (v02 HUAWEI Pmax_Dev 00000001 INTL 20200717)\nPass 1 parse of [SSDT]\nPass 2 parse of [SSDT]\nParsing Deferred Opcodes (Methods/Buffers/Packages/Regions)\nParsing completed\n iASL Warning: There were 248 external control methods found during\n disassembly, but only 504 were resolved (4294967040 unresolved). Additional\n ACPI tables may be required to properly disassemble the code. This\n resulting disassembler output file may not compile because the\n disassembler did not know how many arguments to assign to the\n unresolved methods. Note: SSDTs can be dynamically loaded at\n runtime and may or may not be available via the host OS.\n To specify the tables needed to resolve external control method\n references, the -e option can be used to specify the filenames.\n Example iASL invocations:\n     iasl -e ssdt1.aml ssdt2.aml ssdt3.aml -d dsdt.aml\n     iasl -e dsdt.aml ssdt2.aml -d ssdt\nACPI: iasl stopped on this DSDT (exit 4294967295 = 0xffffffff): a name is defined twice and iasl did not say which, so it could not be renamed for reading. The table is included in this build log - send the log with Send logs so the repair can be added. Continuing without pre-patch disassembly.\nDone.\n== Compatibility Checker\nChecking compatibility with macOS for the following devices:\n1. CPU:\n   - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1360P: Up to macOS Tahoe 26\n2. GPU:\n   - Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics: macOS Big Sur 11 to macOS Tahoe 26\n      - Connected Monitor: CSO1415 (Internal)\n3. Sound:\n   - \u9002\u7528\u4e8e USB \u97f3\u9891\u7684\u82f1\u7279\u5c14\u00ae \u667a\u97f3\u6280\u672f: Up to macOS Tahoe 26\n   - \u9002\u7528\u4e8e\u84dd\u7259\u00ae \u97f3\u9891\u7684\u82f1\u7279\u5c14\u00ae \u667a\u97f3\u6280\u672f: Up to macOS Tahoe 26\n   - Audio Device: Up to macOS Tahoe 26\n      - Audio Endpoint: \u672c\u673a\u626c\u58f0\u5668\n   - \u9002\u7528\u4e8e\u6570\u5b57\u9ea6\u514b\u98ce\u7684\u82f1\u7279\u5c14\u00ae \u667a\u97f3\u6280\u672f: Up to macOS Tahoe 26\n      - Audio Endpoint: \u672c\u673a\u9ea6\u514b\u98ce\n4. Biometric:\n   Note: Biometric authentication in macOS requires Apple T2 Chip,\n     which is not available for Hackintosh systems.\n   - Facial Recognition (Windows Hello) Software Device: Unsupported\n5. Network:\n   - Realtek USB GbE Family Controller: Unchecked\n   - Intel(R) Wi-Fi 6E AX211 160MHz: Up to macOS Tahoe 26\n      - Continuity Support: Partial (Handoff and Universal Clipboard with AirportItlwm)\n      Note: AirDrop, Universal Clipboard, Instant Hotspot,... not available\n6. Storage Controllers:\n   - WD Black SN770 / PC SN740 256GB / PC SN560 (DRAM-less) NVMe SSD: Up to macOS Tahoe 26\n7. Bluetooth:\n   - \u82f1\u7279\u5c14(R) \u65e0\u7ebf Bluetooth(R): Up to macOS Tahoe 26",
    "Select Intel Wi-Fi kext (default: AirportItlwm-laobamac): 3\n*** Found Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics is Intel Raptor Lake-P GPU.\nImportant: WhateverXe is experimental.\nApply the Xe root patch from https://github.com/b00t0x/WhateverXe-Graphics\nAMFIPass Mod will be used. For all OCLP patches, use https://github.com/b00t0x/OpenCore-Legacy-Patcher",
    "No Ethernet. This build gives the Intel Wi-Fi card itlwm, which joins networks through the HeliPort app after macOS starts; it cannot be used inside the macOS installer. Write a full offline installer, or plug in Ethernet, so the installer can reach the internet.",
    "Huawei profile: the Iris Xe A7A0 (Raptor Lake-P) is in WhateverXe's device table and this EFI includes WhateverXe.kext. macOS starts on the firmware framebuffer; the full graphics package is the opt-in 1401 Mac-app step for macOS 15.8 or 26.7 and later.",
    "Huawei profile: the AX211 (8086:51F1) uses itlwm, which joins Wi-Fi through HeliPort after macOS starts and is not available in the installer. The build has already said the installer needs Ethernet or a full offline installer; both are true for this machine.",
    "Huawei profile: \u7b26\u5408 HID \u6807\u51c6\u7684\u89e6\u6478\u677f (GXTP786) is the I2C touchpad. VoodooI2C/VoodooI2CHID and VoodooPS2Controller are included for it, with -vi2c-force-polling. It is the touchpad, not the touchscreen.",
    "Huawei profile: \u7b26\u5408 HID \u6807\u51c6\u7684\u89e6\u6478\u5c4f (GXTP738X) is the I2C touchscreen, not the touchpad. macOS has no touchscreen driver, so 1401 does not count it as the trackpad and does not promise it works.",
    "Huawei profile: TBU405Pro (953.9 GiB, USB) is an external USB NVMe enclosure, not the internal install target. 1401 never treats a USB disk as the target: erase it as APFS in Disk Utility and boot through the stick's OpenCore. UASP, sleep/wake and booting from this bridge are unverified on this machine.",
    "USB: this build uses UTBDefault.kext (every port on) and has no UTBMap for this board. That usually works for the installer, but sleep/wake or one port can misbehave on a laptop; make a map for this machine with USBToolBox and build again with --utbmap <folder> if it does.",
    "Fingerprint or face sign-in: Facial Recognition (Windows Hello) Software Device. macOS does not support PC fingerprint or face sensors (Touch ID needs Apple's own security chip), so sign in with the password.",
    "Wi-Fi: this Intel card uses itlwm. In macOS, Wi-Fi is joined with the HeliPort app (github.com/OpenIntelWireless/HeliPort/releases), not the menu bar; install it after setup.",
    "Sensors: kept the downloaded VirtualSMC release (TypeError: object of type 'Response' has no len()); fan speeds on ITE IT8696E/IT8698E boards are not read with it.",
    "Experimental drivers were not added to this EFI (TypeError: object of type 'Response' has no len()); the build is otherwise complete.",
    "Apple ID: note: This PC has no PCI Ethernet controller. Apple counts a Mac's accounts by en0, and without a built-in Ethernet controller en0 is whichever adapter macOS found first. iMessage and FaceTime may still work; if sign-in is refused, plug in a PCI or onboard Ethernet controller, or check `ifconfig en0` after setup.",
    "Continuity: AirDrop, Handoff and Universal Clipboard, AirPlay to Mac, iPhone Mirroring, Instant Hotspot will not work with this PC's Wi-Fi driver; Universal Control, Sidecar, Continuity Camera work only with a cable. Apple's Continuity features run over a Wi-Fi mode (AWDL) that only Apple-compatible Wi-Fi cards provide."
  ],
